2 CONT Deportation (years) 3
2 CONT Deportation (place): Ukhtizhemlag, Komi ASSR, corrective labor camp
2 CONT Comments: fled from Dąbrowa Tarnowska to the Soviet-occupied territory, 1939; lived in Lesko; apprehended in the village of Olchowce in a group of four people attempting to cross the border from the USSR into the German-occupied territory, 1940
2 CONC ; pre-war Polish documents with photograph (57); birth certificate (60); covered by the amnesty for Polish citizens in 1941; released to Vizinga, Sysolsky District, Komi ASSR, RSFSR (Russia)
