1 NOTE "A Jewish family survives the Holocaust hidden by a Polish family
2 CONT In 1939, when the Second World War broke out, the Stein family escaped Poland. Paula, a polyglot architect, and Meir, a textile industrialist, fled with their only child, Israel, to Vilnius, Lithuania, and later to Bialystok, attempting to sav
2 CONC e themselves from certain death in the extermination camps."
