1 SOUR Jewish Music Research Centre
1 NOTE Rav Shmuel Zalmanov was a Chabad Hasid. He was a yeshiva administrator in Warsaw and Vilna, and the director of the "Nihoah" choir (Chabad Hasidic melodies). He is best known for his editing of the Sefer HaNiggunim. At the request of Rabbi Yose
2 CONC f Yitzchak Schneersohn, the Chabad Rebbe, Zalmanov compiled, corrected, and preserved Chabad melodies. The book includes hundreds of transcriptions and explanatory notes.
2 CONT
2 CONT For more on Zalmanov's work, see: Zigman, Tamar. “Sefer HaNiggunim.” (Hebrew) National Library of Israel Blog, December 7, 2017. https://blog.nli.org.il/nigunim/.
